            <div xml:id="d717">

                <pb facs="0641" n="632" sameAs="frus:frus1940v02/pg632"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123 M 956/293: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Murphy</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Vichy</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-12-18T10:00:00+02:00">December 18,
                            1940—10 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 1:25 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1153. For the Under Secretary. I am departing from Vichy on December 18 by
                    commercial plane for Dakar via Algiers. General Weygand now in Dakar will leave
                    there for Casablanca on December 22 and will receive me on December 21. I shall
                    then return to Algiers, thereafter visiting Tunis, Casablanca, Rabat, and
                    Tangier in the order named, planning to spend 2 or 3 days or longer in each
                    place depending on the circumstances.</p>
                <p>Matthews in charge.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Murphy</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
